<%
// Family Name filter select for a bulk-print member picker - a real
// request: "all bulk printing should have filter by family name." Used
// standalone only by the Name Tag Requests panel now, which never had a
// Type filter to combine it with - every OTHER member-based Design/Print
// panel (Schedule Cards, Name Tags, Name Tags + Schedule Cards front/
// back, Barcodes Only, Barcode Mailing Labels) folded this same Family
// facet into its Type select instead (views/partials/bulk-print-filter-
// select.ejs - a real follow-up request: "there are currently two
// dropdown filters, we only need one, combine them"). Client-side
// filtered against each row's own data-family-id (views/partials/print-
// picker-table.ejs) by public/js/design-print-hub.js's wireBulkMemberList.
// That's deliberately different from the Members/Schedule page's own
// family filter (views/admin-schedule.ejs), which round-trips a real page
// reload - there the whole page (and its own server-side query) is
// scoped to one filter combination at a time; here the panel's full
// member list is already sitting in the DOM (see print-picker-table.ejs's
// own comment on why), so re-filtering it in the browser avoids a reload
// of that same member set. Locals: id (the <select>'s own unique DOM id),
// families (utils/members.js's allFamilies()).
%>
<select class="name-tag-bulk-filter-select" id="<%= id %>">
  <option value="">All Families</option>
  <% families.forEach(function(f) { %>
    <option value="<%= f.id %>"><%= f.name %> Family</option>
  <% }); %>
</select>
